  "notes": "TCL C89B 85\" Google TV, 2024 (device G08, model \"Smart TV Pro\", MediaTek tcl9618), a local variant of the C855\nAndroid 14 (Google TV), firmware UTT2.250416.001 AU02, product G08_4K_GB. Same product and build as\nexamples/tcl-85rm7l-google-tv; that list was the starting point.\n\nApply:   TV_HOST=<tv ip> tools/disable.sh examples/tcl-c89b-google-tv/debloat.txt\nUndo:    TV_HOST=<tv ip> tools/restore.sh examples/tcl-c89b-google-tv/debloat.txt com.google.android.apps.tv.launcherx\nTheme:   TV_HOST=<tv ip> tools/theme.sh examples/tcl-c89b-google-tv   (config.json: Live TV, remote keys)\nEverything is DISABLED, not uninstalled. Comment out any line you want to keep.\n\nTested 2026-10-21 on one set on Ethernet, applied in batches with screenshots between them: Home, the\nInputs menu (HDMI 1-4 and Live TV), the Chromecast, AirPlay and Miracast processes, and the remote's\ngear, Netflix, Prime Video and YouTube buttons worked; the disabled set was identical after a reboot,\nand HomeKeyService bound on its own after another once AUTO_START was saved. One day of use, not weeks.\n\nConnection: USB debugging alone opens port 5555 on Ethernet. Wireless debugging switches itself back off\nthere: Android only enables it on Wi-Fi.\n\nLauncher, in this order: launcher/build-and-install.sh with STOCK_LAUNCHER=none (installs it, then stops\nwith an error because Home stays on launcherx), then this list (setupwraith is listed before launcherx, so the wizard never gets Home;\nit owned no saved network here), then enable HomeKeyService with the settings command\nbuild-and-install.sh runs for HOME_KEY_SERVICE=1.\nTclAppBoot blocks HomeKeyService at every boot until the launcher has AUTO_START, saved to disk:\nTV_HOST=<tv ip> tools/venv/bin/python -I tools/tv.py 'appops set com.gathin.tvhome AUTO_START allow; appops write-settings'\n\nRemote (BT_RC933_U1): every TCL button arrives on scancode 240 and TCL's own key table picks the keycode,\nso config.json matches keycodes: gear 83, Netflix 4062, Prime Video 4099, YouTube 190 (BUTTON_3). The\nowner pointed 190 at SmartTube (org.smarttube.stable). The Input button works without a service. Info,\nTV and LIST are Live TV keys and do nothing on Home.\n\nKept: Chromecast, AirPlay, Miracast, Google Assistant (katniss), com.google.android.tv.remote.service (the\nremote's mic), the USB media player and gallery, com.tcl.tv, com.tcl.suspension, and Netflix, Prime\nVideo and Disney+.\nTCL tracking and analytics",
